### Reproduction steps

Create a TypeScript file with the following contents, then follow the instructions in the comments:

```ts
/**
 * Press Ctrl+space after the `g` in {@linkcode g}  <-- should suggest `greet`
* Cltr+click on {@linkcode greet} does nagivate to the `greet method.`
 */
class Person {
   constructor(private name: string) {

   }

   greet(): string {
      return 'Hello ' + this.name;  // Crl+space after just `this.n` does suggest "name"
   }
}

const p = new Person('Zed');
p.greet();

/**
 * Press Ctrl+space after the `g`: {@linkcode Person#g}  <-- should suggest `greet`
 */
```


### Current vs. Expected behavior

Current behavior: nothing happens when pressing Ctrl+Space as indicated.

Expected: suggest matching symbols ("greet" in this case)

### Zed version and system specs

Zed: v0.231.1+stable.213.e71b6aa44ffaac9bdaf986288289359e6f1b3572 (Zed) 
OS: Linux Wayland tuxedo 24.04
Memory: 62.5 GiB
Architecture: x86_64
GPU: Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (ADL GT2) || Intel open-source Mesa driver || Mesa 25.2.8-1~24.04-tux1
